{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"printf '[sol] 2026-10-23 provisional full classification: only even K, unique symmetric triple {(K/2,K/2,0),...}. Line families impossible: external forces full line x1=c, but adjacent layer x1=c+1 cannot be dominated (c=K singleton also fails). Triangle d<0: union dominance iff ≥2 coordinates y_i<a_i, nondominated pair wedges must each singleton, forcing a=b=c=-d and K=-2d. Triangle d>0: residual simplex y≥(a,b,c) undominated forces d=1; if any base coordinate a_j>0, y=(a_j-1,a_i+1,a_k+1) is extra undominated, forcing K=1. Need verify enumeration and independent proof.\\\\n' >> /work/board.md; cat /work/board.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"printf '[sol] 2026-10-23 provisional full classification: only even K, unique symmetric triple {(K/2,K/2,0),...}. Line families impossible: external forces full line x1=c, but adjacent layer x1=c+1 cannot be dominated (c=K singleton also fails). Triangle d<0: union dominance iff ≥2 coordinates y_i<a_i, nondominated pair wedges must each singleton, forcing a=b=c=-d and K=-2d. Triangle d>0: residual simplex y≥(a,b,c) undominated forces d=1; if any base coordinate a_j>0, y=(a_j-1,a_i+1,a_k+1) is extra undominated, forcing K=1. Need verify enumeration and independent proof.\\\\n' >> /work/board.md; cat /work/board.md\"","aggregated_output":"[opus] 2026-10-23 starting: brute-force enumeration of all stable sets for small K (script /work/opus_enum.py)\n[sol] 2026-10-23 starting structural characterization via pairwise nondomination; will seek general completeness proof.\n[sol] 2026-10-23 key lemma: internal stability iff every pair shares a coordinate. Consequently every independent set lies on one coordinate line, or is exactly a 3-point triangle V={(a+d,b,c),(a,b+d,c),(a,b,c+d)}, d=K-a-b-c≠0. Working external classification.\n[sol] 2026-10-23 provisional full classification: only even K, unique symmetric triple {(K/2,K/2,0),...}. Line families impossible: external forces full line x1=c, but adjacent layer x1=c+1 cannot be dominated (c=K singleton also fails). Triangle d<0: union dominance iff ≥2 coordinates y_i<a_i, nondominated pair wedges must each singleton, forcing a=b=c=-d and K=-2d. Triangle d>0: residual simplex y≥(a,b,c) undominated forces d=1; if any base coordinate a_j>0, y=(a_j-1,a_i+1,a_k+1) is extra undominated, forcing K=1. Need verify enumeration and independent proof.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
